          <feedback>Stage 1 executed as expected. Execute modified exactly one model file, blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/PoemNew.bml, and touched no _meta/transform/ ModelTransformation files. Changes are coherent and self-consistent: the `&lt;is>` summary was updated from 'translated into Russian from German, about a tree and a mushroom' to 'written in German, about a tree and a mushroom'; the `&lt;documentation>` body was replaced with a 4-stanza original German poem about a beech tree (Buche) and a mushroom (Pilz), matching the tree+mushroom theme; the `&lt;title>` property was updated from the Russian 'Дерево и гриб' to the German 'Im Schatten der Buche', consistent with the new content. The `&lt;author>` value ('John Doe') and all surrounding structure (name, type, baseType, properties layout) were preserved. Stanza count (4) and general structure are unchanged from the prior version. No validation was run in this Reflect step (read-only), but the diff is structurally sound BML with balanced tags. One minor note: the closing quote in the third stanza uses a straight double-quote (&quot;) to close a German opening quote („), a slight typographic inconsistency, but it is inside documentation text and harmless.</feedback>
